  "worked_solution": "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. Writing $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=\\sqrt{x-2}$ in terms of $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={x}^{2} & \\,\u27f9\\,x=\\sqrt{y} \\\\ y=\\sqrt{x-2} & \\,\u27f9\\,x={y}^{2}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14055472/assets/bb3249a9580e754c4ef9c33239c2a51a9b57ca9032a6acbeef7bbc532b2d4345.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\sqrt{y}\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}\\frac{xy}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y}}^{{y}^{2}+2}\\frac{xy}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
